node_modules
# The committed 50-state bank (E-6): `data/us-states/` is tracked, and is
# reproduced byte-for-byte by `bun run build -- --offline --out data/us-states`
# from the committed fixture — that offline rebuild is what a passing
# `bun test` checks (`src/committed-bank.test.ts`, describe block "T-010
# criteria 6 and 8 — the tracked bytes are what an offline rebuild produces",
# which actually spawns the CLI offline twice and diffs the bytes).
# Everything else under data/ stays ignored — ad hoc --out targets, subsets,
# and anything the *live* pipeline writes into data/us-states/ itself that is
# not part of the bank. `!data/us-states` un-ignores the whole directory, so
# `fun-facts.review.json` — which a default, non-`--offline` run writes there
# with unreviewed, `reviewed: false` Wikipedia prose (CLAUDE.md "Content
# rules") — needs its own re-ignore below rather than relying on `data/*`.
data/*
!data/us-states
data/us-states/*.review.json
